# WhatsApp OTP sign-in (s3.0.107)

Resume: `@whatsapp-otp$` / `$wa-otp$`.

## Welcome card contract (`index.html#landingPage`)

Order: Google → Microsoft → Facebook → Email → **Continue with WhatsApp OTP (Worldwide)** → **Continue with SMS OTP (US Only)** → `#authStatus` → `.login-legal` (Privacy Policy · Do Not Sell or Share, white, last line of the card).

- No "Or use One Time Password (OTP) via SMS" divider.
- SMS panel country select = `+1 United States` only (Firebase phone auth + reCAPTCHA; unchanged backend).
- WhatsApp panel owns the full country list.
- OTP explanation lives in the Welcome `?` (`help-welcome`) — EN in `index.html` + `floqai-help-repository.js` + `scripts/_help-en.json`, 10 locales in `floqr-i18n-help.js`.
- Chrome keys: `app.whatsappOtp`, `app.smsOtp`, `app.privacyPolicy`, `app.doNotSell`, `otp.*` (all 11 packs).

## Backend (`functions/whatsapp-otp-functions.js`, pure helpers `whatsapp-otp-core.js`)

| Callable | Does |
|---|---|
| `requestWhatsAppOtp({phone})` | E.164 check → per-IP limit (`otpRateLimits`, 12/h) → per-phone challenge (`whatsappOtpChallenges/{sha256}`, 60 s cooldown, 5/h) → HMAC code hash (pepper `CLUB_AUTH_CODE_PEPPER`) → Twilio Messages API to `whatsapp:+…` → poll message status ~5 s → fail loudly on `failed/undelivered` (challenge voided) |
| `verifyWhatsAppOtp({phone, code, challengeId})` | Transaction: not used/voided, not expired (5 min), attempts < 5, constant-time hash compare → delete hash → `getUserByPhoneNumber` or `createUser({phoneNumber})` → custom token `{whatsappOtp: true}` |

Same phone = same Firebase uid as SMS phone auth.

Sender: `TWILIO_WHATSAPP_FROM` secret (fallback `TWILIO_FROM_NUMBER`). Credentials: `TWILIO_ACCOUNT_SID`, `TWILIO_AUTH_TOKEN`.

### Meta / Twilio requirement (production)

Business-initiated WhatsApp outside a 24 h customer session **requires an approved template**. OTP must use the **Authentication** category (copy-code button).

1. Twilio Console → Messaging → Senders → WhatsApp: register FLOQR's WhatsApp Business sender (not the sandbox).
2. Content Template Builder → type **WhatsApp Authentication**, variable `{{1}}` = code → submit for Meta approval.
3. Put the `HX…` Content SID in `functions/.env` as `TWILIO_WHATSAPP_OTP_CONTENT_SID=HX…` (param, not a secret) and redeploy the two callables.

Without the Content SID the callable sends a free-form body — works only in the Twilio sandbox (recipient sent the join word) or inside a 24 h session. Twilio error `63016` = template required; `63015` = sandbox join missing; `63007` = sender not WhatsApp-enabled. `explainWhatsAppError` maps these to patron copy.

## Compliance logging

All via `functions/twilio-log.js` with `forceSecurity: true` (every row also lands in `twilioComplianceLogs`, 7-year retention):

| purpose | collection | when |
|---|---|---|
| `auth-otp` | `twilioWhatsAppLogs` | Twilio accept / reject (body = code redacted, or `[WhatsApp template HX…]`) |
| `auth-otp-status` | `twilioWhatsAppLogs` | Polled delivery status + Twilio error code |
| `auth-otp-verify` | `twilioFeatureLogs` | `verified` / `rejected` / `expired` / `locked` (+ `actorUid` on success) |

Every row carries `extra.consent = {type: "user-initiated", surface, notice: "otp.whatsappNote"}`. Phones are masked + hashed; codes never stored in clear (`redactSecrets` masks 6-digit runs). Master Admin → Twilio tabs show them.

